@thread good_year
# en: The Good Year
name [86224e] = 好年景
# en: Seven good harvests running in the valley, and everyone so glad to see a stranger.
premise [9d3fe2] = 山谷里连着七年好收成，人人都那么高兴见到陌生人。
# en: The harvest board by the market cross got its seventh good mark of seven, and the whole green cheered. The landlord said a visitor in a seventh year was luck.
journal.1 [330b67] = 集市十字碑旁的收成板上画下了七年里第七道好记号，整片绿地都欢呼起来。客栈老板说，第七年来个访客，那是福气。
# en: At the coaching inn you met Ottilie Venn, a fern-hunter from the capital, lodging in room seven for nothing.
journal.2 [7e70fd] = 你在驿站客栈遇见了奥蒂莉·维恩，一个从首都来的寻蕨人，白住七号房。
# en: The inn's guest book: every seventh harvest, one guest who "stays on", and never leaves.
journal.3 [a45deb] = 客栈的住客簿：每逢第七个收获季，就有一位客人“住下了”，再没离开。
# en: The scarecrows' coats have names in their collars: the names of guests who stayed on.
journal.4 [52f1c2] = 稻草人外套的领子里缝着名字：都是那些“住下了”的客人。
# en: The miller counts the dry wheel's turns for "the supper", and calls it an old arrangement.
journal.5 [ecb56a] = 磨坊主数着空转的水车转了多少圈，等着“那场晚宴”，还管它叫老规矩。
# en: Mrs Quill prints a harvest page every seventh year, with a blank for "the Guest of the Year". The keepers cut it out.
journal.6 [2c3d7f] = 奎尔太太每逢第七年印一页收获页，上面留着一行空白给“年度之客”。守约人会把它剪掉。
# en: The man in good boots has bought the old hall.
journal.7 [7db6ed] = 那个穿好靴子的人买下了老宅邸。
# en: In the old hall you read the agent's plan: a guest every year instead of every seventh, if the luck follows his company's land.
journal.8 [e7621c] = 你在老宅邸里读到了代理人的计划：不是七年一位客人，而是每年一位，只要福气跟着他公司的地走。
# en: Ottilie is gone, and the inn says she never came.
journal.9 [fba01d] = 奥蒂莉不见了，客栈却说她从没来过。
# en: The Tenant under the hollow hill keeps every guest the valley ever lent it at its supper. Its door opens to one who knows.
journal.10 [07da90] = 空心山下的山中房客把山谷借给它的每一位客人都留在它的晚宴上。它的门只为知情的人打开。
# en: You broke the valley's bargain in the Tenant's own hall.
journal.11 [9d6b50] = 你在山中房客自己的大厅里毁掉了山谷的约定。
# en: You offered the Tenant better company than one lent stranger, and it took the offer.
journal.12 [65c0f7] = 你给了山中房客比一个被借出去的陌生人更好的陪伴，它接受了。
# en: You gave the Tenant the agent's offer.
journal.13 [1dbbaa] = 你把代理人的条件交给了山中房客。

@event gy_seventh_year
# en: The Seventh Column
title [abd05d] = 第七栏
# en: The whole green is out round a {season == "winter": bonfire|trestle of cider} at the market cross, toasting the harvest board: the landlord of the coaching inn has chalked the year's mark, the seventh in the seventh column, all good. {at_home(): Your neighbours raise their cups to it, and then, every one, look across at the travellers in the inn yard, and away.|The landlord turns, sees you, and beams. "And a visitor! In a seventh year! Now that's luck."}
text [3c0f48] = 整片绿地的人都聚在集市十字碑旁，围着一堆{season == "winter": 篝火|摆满苹果酒的长桌}，为收成板举杯：驿站客栈的老板刚用粉笔画下今年的记号，第七栏的第七道，全是好年景。{at_home(): 你的邻居们举杯致意，然后一个接一个地朝客栈院子里的旅人望一眼，又移开目光。|老板转过身，看见你，笑逐颜开。“还有位访客！在第七年！这可是福气。”}
# en: A village green, a crowd cheering round an old chalk tally board nailed to a market cross, a beaming innkeeper chalking a mark, a student at the edge of the crowd.
scene [c0dac8] = 村中绿地，一群人围着钉在集市十字碑上的旧粉笔计数板欢呼，满面笑容的客栈老板正在画记号，一个学生站在人群边上。
# en: Drink to the seventh
opt.left.label [aa4f68] = 为第七年干杯
# en: {at_home(): You stand a round and drink to the seventh with your neighbours. It's warm and loud and happy, and nobody once asks after the travellers at the inn, and everybody is careful not to look at them.|You stand a round and drink to the seventh with the whole green. It's warm and loud and happy, and everyone is very kind, and at the end of it you can't remember a single person asking you where you were going next. Only how long you were staying.}
opt.left.say.1 [8d4452] = {at_home(): 你请了一轮酒，和邻居们一起为第七年干杯。温暖、热闹、快乐，没有一个人问起客栈里的旅人，每个人都小心地不去看他们。|你请了一轮酒，和整片绿地的人一起为第七年干杯。温暖、热闹、快乐，每个人都非常和善，到最后你想不起有谁问过你接下来要去哪儿。他们只问你要待多久。}
# en: Ask what's lucky about seven
opt.right.label [6af1ea] = 问问七有什么吉利
# en: "Seven good years," says the landlord, "and every one a gift." Somebody starts a song before you can ask what the gift is for. Walking back, you notice the eighth column on the board has been ruled already, neat and empty, and the chalk by it is new.
opt.right.say.1 [24073d] = “七个好年头，”老板说，“每一年都是一份礼。”你还没来得及问这份礼是拿什么换的，就有人唱起了歌。往回走时，你注意到收成板上的第八栏已经画好了格子，整整齐齐，空着，旁边的粉笔是新的。

@event gy_fern_hunter
# en: The Fern-Hunter
title [a50a9e] = 寻蕨人
# en: At the inn's best table a young woman in a battered sun hat is pressing ferns into a book the size of a doorstep: Ottilie Venn, a fern-hunter from the capital. "The landlord's given me room seven for nothing," she says, delighted. "The best room. Because it's a seventh year, he says. Isn't that funny?" {not at_home() and not flag(marsh_rue) and seen(market_inn_welcome) > 0: The landlord asked you, too, how long you were staying.|}
text [1be464] = 客栈最好的那张桌子边，一个戴着破旧遮阳帽的年轻女人正把蕨叶压进一本门槛那么厚的书里：奥蒂莉·维恩，从首都来的寻蕨人。“老板白给我住七号房，”她高兴地说，“最好的房间。说是因为今年是第七年。好笑吧？”{not at_home() and not flag(marsh_rue) and seen(market_inn_welcome) > 0: 老板也问过你要待多久。|}
# en: A cheerful young woman in a sun hat and boots at a coaching inn table, pressing ferns between the pages of a fat book, a student sitting down opposite her.
scene [cbdb20] = 驿站客栈的桌边，一个戴遮阳帽、穿靴子的开朗年轻女人正把蕨叶夹进一本厚书里，一个学生在她对面坐下。
# en: Go out with her after ferns
opt.left.label [7f3d1e] = 跟她出去找蕨
# en: You spend the afternoon {season == "winter": in the snowy fen with Ottilie, digging out the brown crowns of royal ferns,|up to your knees in the fen with Ottilie,} and she knows the name of everything green and laughs at everything else. You come back soaked to the thigh and fond of her. At the inn door the landlord is waiting with towels, as if he knew when you'd be back.
opt.left.say.1 [ab9b3d] = 你和奥蒂莉在{season == "winter": 积雪的沼地里待了一下午，挖出紫萁褐色的根冠，|沼地里蹚了一下午，水没到膝盖，}她叫得出每一样绿东西的名字，别的什么都能让她笑。你回来时湿到大腿，也喜欢上了她。客栈门口，老板拿着毛巾等着，好像他早知道你们什么时候回来。
# en: Tell her to mind the inn's kindness
opt.right.label [920649] = 提醒她留心客栈的好意
# en: "Mind it?" Ottilie laughs. "I'm going to frame it." She won't be warned, kindly and completely, and talks about ferns instead. You leave feeling foolish, and then, at the inn door, when the landlord smiles at you both, not foolish at all.
opt.right.say.1 [d0666e] = “留心？”奥蒂莉笑了，“我要把它裱起来。”她和和气气、彻彻底底地不听劝，转头聊起了蕨。你离开时觉得自己傻；然后在客栈门口，老板冲你们俩微笑的时候，又一点也不觉得了。

@event gy_guest_book
# en: The Guest Book
title [698f89] = 住客簿
# en: {seen(gy_guest_book) > 1: The guest book's out on the counter again, and the landlord's down in the cellar again.|The landlord's gone down to the cellar, and the inn's guest book is lying open on the counter: a fat old thing, signatures going back further than the inn's sign. Every name has a date in, and a date out, in the landlord's hand.}
text [e1f726] = {seen(gy_guest_book) > 1: 住客簿又摊在柜台上，老板又下地窖去了。|老板下地窖去了，客栈的住客簿摊开在柜台上：一本厚厚的旧册子，签名比客栈的招牌还要古老。每个名字后面都有入住和离开的日子，是老板的笔迹。}
# en: A thick old guest book open on a coaching inn's counter by a lamp, columns of signatures going back generations, a student turning its pages while the landlord is down in the cellar.
scene [2761d3] = 驿站客栈柜台上一盏灯旁摊开一本厚重的旧住客簿，一栏栏签名延续了好几代人，老板在地窖里，一个学生正在翻页。
# en: Leave it and wait for your pint
opt.left.label [378dde] = 别碰它，等你的酒
# en: You don't touch it, and pay for your pint like an honest guest. The landlord comes up with your pint, sees where you're standing, and closes the book, smiling, and puts it under the counter.
opt.left.say.1 [73a982] = 你没碰它，像个老实客人一样付了酒钱。老板端着你的酒上来，看见你站在哪儿，笑着合上册子，放到柜台底下。
# en: Read back through it
opt.right.label [3ed33e] = 往回翻着读
# en: Years and years of names, in and out. But every seventh harvest there's one guest with no date out, only two words beside the name in the landlord's hand: "stays on". Seven years before that, another. And the last page of this year has a line already ruled, waiting.
opt.right.say.1 [82ef28] = 一年又一年的名字，来了又走。可每逢第七个收获季，就有一位客人没有离开的日子，名字旁只有老板写的几个字：“住下了”。再往前七年，又是一个。而今年的最后一页，已经画好了一行，空着等人。
# en: You've barely turned a page when the cellar door opens. "Our visitors," says the landlord fondly, taking the book from under your hands. "We keep them all." He puts it away, and pours your pint, and doesn't charge you for it.
opt.right.say.2 [c028dd] = 你才翻过一页，地窖门就开了。“我们的客人们，”老板亲切地说，把册子从你手底下抽走，“我们每一位都留着。”他把册子收好，给你倒了酒，没收钱。

@event gy_scarecrow_names
# en: Names in the Collars
title [b92d03] = 领子里的名字
# en: The scarecrows stand in their row along the far field, in their very decent coats: good wool, brass buttons, a travelling cloak. Somebody's coats, once. {seen(fields_scarecrow_coats) > 1: You found a tailor's label in one collar before. In the dusk you see that every collar has a name in it, a little name-tape, the kind a careful mother sews in.|In the dusk you see that every collar has a little name-tape stitched inside, the kind a careful mother sews in.}
text [2dfe07] = 稻草人沿着远处的田边站成一排，穿着相当体面的外套：好羊毛、黄铜扣子，还有一件旅行斗篷。曾经是谁的外套。{seen(fields_scarecrow_coats) > 1: 你以前在一件领子里找到过裁缝的标签。暮色里你看见每件领子里都有一个名字，一小条名牌，是细心的母亲会缝上的那种。|暮色里你看见每件领子内侧都缝着一小条名牌，是细心的母亲会缝上的那种。}
# en: A row of scarecrows in fine old travelling coats along a field's edge at dusk, a student turning down the collar of one to read a name stitched inside.
scene [a86f15] = 黄昏时田边一排稻草人穿着精致的旧旅行外套，一个学生翻开其中一件的领子，读缝在里面的名字。
# en: Read every collar down the row
opt.left.label [9ae6ae] = 把整排领子都读一遍
# en: {flag(gy_guest_book): You go down the row in the dew till your feet are soaked and cold. Every name is one from the guest book, one with "stays on" beside it, a coat for every seven years, back further than the hedges.|You go down the row in the dew till your feet are soaked and cold, reading names: a dozen strangers, and the coats getting older as you go, back to a cloak your grandmother would have called old-fashioned.}
opt.left.say.1 [72544a] = {flag(gy_guest_book): 你踩着露水沿着那一排走下去，直到脚湿透冰凉。每个名字都在住客簿里，旁边都写着“住下了”，七年一件外套，比树篱还要古老。|你踩着露水沿着那一排走下去，直到脚湿透冰凉，一路读着名字：十几个陌生人，外套越往后越旧，一直到一件你祖母都会嫌老派的斗篷。}
# en: Leave the coats alone
opt.right.label [f2ce14] = 别动那些外套
# en: You put the collar straight and leave them. All the way back to the lane you feel the row of them behind you, the sleeves moving all together in the wind.
opt.right.say.1 [088c22] = 你把领子翻正，走开了。一路回到小路上，你都感觉那一排在你身后，袖子在风里齐齐地摆动。

@event gy_miller_tally
# en: The Miller's Tally
title [cf8b51] = 磨坊主的计数
# en: The wheel's turning on the dry race again, and the miller's on his chair beside it with a lantern and a little book, making a mark at every turn, as patient as a man counting sheep. The book looks just like the landlord's.
text [7d36b6] = 水车又在干涸的水渠上转起来了，磨坊主坐在一旁的椅子上，提着灯笼拿着小本子，每转一圈就画一道，耐心得像个数羊的人。那本子和客栈老板的一模一样。
# en: An old miller on a chair by a turning waterwheel over a dry millrace at dusk, writing tally marks in a small book by lantern light, a student on the bridge.
scene [0972c7] = 黄昏，一个老磨坊主坐在干涸水渠上转动的水车旁，借着灯笼的光在小本子上画计数，一个学生站在桥上。
# en: Ask him what he's counting
opt.left.label [1c5bc8] = 问他在数什么
# en: "Turns to the supper," he says, as if you'd know. "Seven years of turns, and then the supper, and the guest goes in, and the wheel rests." He looks at you a long while. "Nobody's hurt by it. They come back." Then he looks at you, and you watch him remember {at_home(): whose child you are|that you're a stranger}, and he closes the book.
opt.left.say.1 [b39999] = “数到晚宴的圈数，”他说，好像你该知道似的。“七年的圈数，然后是晚宴，客人进去，水车就歇了。”他看了你好一会儿。“没人因此受伤。他们会回来的。”然后他又看着你，你看着他想起了{at_home(): 你是谁家的孩子|你是个外乡人}，他合上了本子。
# en: "Valley business," he says pleasantly, and keeps counting, and doesn't look up again however long you stand there. Eventually you go.
opt.left.say.2 [af5fee] = “山谷里的事，”他和气地说，接着数，不管你站多久都没再抬头。最后你走了。
# en: Sit and count with him
opt.right.label [628091] = 坐下陪他一起数
# en: You sit on the cold step and count with him till midnight. He doesn't explain, and you don't ask. The wheel stops, at last, all at once, and he says "Good," to it, like you'd say it to a dog, and goes in.
opt.right.say.1 [21ab7f] = 你坐在冰冷的台阶上陪他数到半夜。他不解释，你也不问。最后水车一下子停了，他对它说了声“好”，就像对狗说的那样，然后进屋去了。

@event gy_almanac_page
# en: The Harvest Page
title [1edd84] = 收获页
# en: Mrs Quill is alone at the press, ink to the elbows. {flag(almanac_pages_counted): She knows you've been in the attic with Nessa; she doesn't say so.|} She sees you looking at the drawer under the press, and after a while she opens it: a stack of loose pages, one for every seventh year, each headed HARVEST SUPPER, each with a line printed for "the Guest of the Year", and a name inked in by hand.
text [286696] = 奎尔太太独自在印刷机旁，墨水沾到了手肘。{flag(almanac_pages_counted): 她知道你和奈莎去过阁楼；她没说破。|}她看见你在看印刷机下面的抽屉，过了一会儿把它拉开：一叠散页，每逢第七年一张，每张的标题都是“收获晚宴”，每张都印着一行“年度之客”，旁边有人用墨水手写了一个名字。
# en: An ink-stained woman at an old hand press in a cramped print shop, holding up a single printed page with a blank line on it, a drawer of identical pages open beside her, a student reading.
scene [8fdbeb] = 狭窄的印刷铺里，一个满手墨迹的女人站在老式手动印刷机旁，举着一张印着空白行的书页，旁边开着一抽屉一模一样的书页，一个学生在读。
# en: Ask why she prints it
opt.left.label [375d87] = 问她为什么印它
# en: "Because they ask," she says, "and then they cut it out, and I put it in the drawer." She closes it. "My mother did, and hers. I tell myself it's only printing." She goes back to the press and doesn't look at you again, and her hands aren't steady.
opt.left.say.1 [ebecf4] = “因为他们要，”她说，“然后他们把它剪掉，我就放进抽屉里。”她关上抽屉。“我母亲这么做，她母亲也是。我跟自己说那只是印东西。”她回到印刷机前，再没看你，她的手在抖。
# en: Take one of the pages
opt.right.label [8ae86c] = 拿走其中一页
# en: You take the oldest page while her back is turned to the press, and she sees, in the type-case's brass, and lets you. Walking out with it inside your coat feels like stealing from somebody who wanted you to.
opt.right.say.1 [83b16f] = 趁她背对着你转向印刷机，你拿了最旧的一页；她在铅字盒的黄铜上看见了，由着你拿。把它揣在外套里走出去，感觉就像从一个希望你偷的人那儿偷东西。

@event gy_agent_drovers
# en: The Agent at the Drovers' Inn
title [8ef2ae] = 赶畜人客栈里的代理人
# en: The man in good boots is drinking with his clerk at the end of the Drovers' Inn's long table, his leather folder at his elbow. {flag(fennick_agent_refused): "I said I'd remember you," he says.|He looks up and smiles at you, a practised smile.} "Sit. I've bought the old hall, and I'm buying the upland. A word to the wise: the valley's luck is about to change hands. Tell me who the inn's guest is this year, and when they go up the hill, and you'll find me generous."
text [582262] = 那个穿好靴子的人正和他的书记员坐在赶畜人客栈长桌的一头喝酒，皮文件夹放在手肘边。{flag(fennick_agent_refused): “我说过我会记住你的，”他说。|他抬头冲你一笑，笑得很老练。}“坐。我买下了老宅邸，还在收购高地。给聪明人一句话：山谷的福气就要换主人了。告诉我今年客栈的客人是谁，他们什么时候上山，你会发现我很大方。”
# en: A well-dressed man in good city boots and his clerk drinking at the end of a rough inn table among drovers, a leather folder at his elbow, smiling up at a student.
scene [473958] = 一个穿着城里好靴子、衣着讲究的男人和他的书记员坐在赶畜人中间一张粗木长桌的一头喝酒，手肘边放着皮文件夹，抬头冲一个学生微笑。
# en: Take his money
opt.left.label [1d5b56] = 收下他的钱
# en: {flag(gy_met_ottilie): You tell him about Ottilie, and room seven.|You tell him the landlord keeps his best room for a guest, and that you'll find out whose.} He writes it in his folder and pays in gold, more than the words were worth. "The old hall," he says, "if you've more." You walk out into the night with the gold heavy and something else heavier.
opt.left.say.1 [4b5830] = {flag(gy_met_ottilie): 你把奥蒂莉和七号房的事告诉了他。|你告诉他，客栈老板把最好的房间留给一位客人，你会查出是谁。}他把它写进文件夹，付了金币，比这几句话值的多得多。“老宅邸，”他说，“要是你还有消息的话。”你走进夜色里，金币沉甸甸的，还有别的什么更沉。
# en: Turn him down, and listen
opt.right.label [cd4048] = 拒绝他，然后听着
# en: You tell him you've nothing to sell. He shrugs and turns back to his clerk, and you sit near enough to hear the rest: the old hall, the papers in it, "the arrangement" and how it might be "improved". You leave with a sour taste and the road to the hall in your head.
opt.right.say.1 [8c0817] = 你告诉他你没什么可卖的。他耸耸肩，转回去跟书记员说话，你坐得够近，听见了剩下的：老宅邸，里面的文件，“老规矩”，以及它可以怎样“改进”。你带着一嘴苦味离开，脑子里记着去老宅邸的路。

@event old_hall_gates
# en: The Shut Hall
title [ac3fed] = 封闭的宅邸
# en: {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: The old hall again, shuttered, the agent's carriage in the drive, the caretaker raking.|Behind its wall at the moor's edge the old hall stands shuttered, as it has since the family went away, nobody in the villages will say when. There's a city carriage in the drive now, and an old caretaker raking leaves that keep coming.}
text [22e537] = {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: 又是老宅邸，百叶窗紧闭，代理人的马车停在车道上，看门人在扫落叶。|荒原边上，老宅邸立在围墙后面，百叶窗紧闭，自从那家人离开就一直这样，可村里没人肯说是什么时候。如今车道上停着一辆城里的马车，一个老看门人在扫怎么也扫不完的落叶。}
# en: A shuttered old manor behind a high wall and iron gates on the edge of a moor, a city carriage in the drive, an old caretaker raking leaves, a student at the gate.
scene [a88dd5] = 荒原边上，高墙和铁门后一座百叶窗紧闭的老庄园，车道上停着城里的马车，一个老看门人在扫落叶，一个学生站在门口。
# en: Talk to the caretaker
opt.left.label [550747] = 和看门人聊聊
# en: {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: You give the caretaker a coin and he talks about the weather, and then, low, about the new master's papers, laid out on the old master's desk "as if he'd been here all his life".|You give the caretaker a coin for his trouble. The old family, he says, kept the valley's books once, "the ones that matter", and sold up and went away in a bad year. The new master's reading them now.}
opt.left.say.1 [7e29f0] = {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: 你给了看门人一枚硬币，他先聊天气，然后压低声音说起新主人的文件，摊在老主人的书桌上，“好像他在这儿住了一辈子似的”。|你给了看门人一枚硬币，算是辛苦钱。他说，老主人家从前替山谷记账，“记那些要紧的账”，后来在一个坏年景里卖了家业走了。新主人现在正在读那些账。}
# en: Walk the wall
opt.right.label [504629] = 沿着围墙走一圈
# en: {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: You walk the wall and find the place where the ivy will hold a climber, and where the study window doesn't latch. Brambles take their toll.|You walk the whole wall through brambles and nettles, and learn its gaps, and the dark window round the back where a lamp burns at night over a desk.}
opt.right.say.1 [880871] = {seen(old_hall_gates) > 1: 你沿着围墙走，找到了常春藤撑得住人的地方，还有书房那扇关不严的窗。荆棘让你付了代价。|你穿过荆棘和荨麻把整道围墙走了一圈，摸清了它的缺口，还有屋后那扇黑窗，夜里有盏灯照着一张书桌。}

@event gy_hall_papers
# en: The Agent's Desk
title [410c48] = 代理人的书桌
# en: {seen(gy_hall_papers) > 1: The old hall again after dark, the back window, the lamp, the desk.|The old hall after dark.} Through the back window, unlatched, there's the study: the old family's ledgers on the shelves, and on the desk the agent's maps of the upland farms, every one he's bought shaded in, and a letter half written.
text [e2b357] = {seen(gy_hall_papers) > 1: 又是天黑后的老宅邸，后窗，灯，书桌。|天黑后的老宅邸。}透过没闩上的后窗就是书房：架子上是老主人家的账册，书桌上是代理人画的高地农场地图，他买下的每一块都涂了阴影，还有一封写了一半的信。
# en: A dark wood-panelled study in an old manor at night, a desk covered in maps and letters under a shaded lamp, a student reading by its light, a dog asleep by the cold hearth.
scene [99810d] = 夜里老庄园中一间深色木板墙的书房，一盏罩着灯罩的灯下，书桌上铺满地图和信件，一个学生借着灯光阅读，一条狗睡在冷掉的壁炉边。
# en: Leave it and go
opt.left.label [204cde] = 别碰，走吧
# en: You leave the window as you found it and go home across the moor's edge, and all the way the lamp in the study burns at your back.
opt.left.say.1 [fb9ed5] = 你让窗户保持原样，沿着荒原边上走回家，一路上书房的灯都在你背后亮着。
# en: Climb in and read
opt.right.label [66e900] = 爬进去读
# en: The old ledgers are the guest book's twin: every seventh name, written by the keepers of a hundred years. The agent's letter, to his principals uptown, is plainer: "The arrangement may be improved. A guest each year, from our own hand, and the luck to follow the company's land." You put it back exactly as it was.
opt.right.say.1 [fc1e0d] = 那些旧账册和住客簿是一对孪生子：每第七个名字，都出自一百年来守约人的手笔。代理人写给城里上家的信说得更直白：“老规矩可以改进。每年一位客人，由我们亲手挑选，福气跟着公司的地走。”你把一切原样放回。
# en: The old dog by the hearth isn't as asleep as it looked. You leave by the window much faster than you came, with its teeth in your trouser leg and the caretaker's lamp coming down the stairs.
opt.right.say.2 [bd30d5] = 壁炉边那条老狗并不像看上去睡得那么沉。你从窗户逃出去，比进来时快得多，裤腿上挂着它的牙，看门人的灯正从楼梯上下来。
# en: Open the desk drawer properly
opt.up.label [97390d] = 好好撬开书桌抽屉
# en: You pick the desk drawer and find the whole correspondence: the agent's letter to his principals, "a guest each year, from our own hand, and the luck to follow the company's land", and their answer: "Proceed." You lock it all away again.
opt.up.say.1 [4f39db] = 你撬开书桌抽屉，找到了全部往来信件：代理人写给上家的信，“每年一位客人，由我们亲手挑选，福气跟着公司的地走”，以及他们的回信：“照办。”你把一切重新锁好。
# en: A pick snaps in the drawer's lock with a crack, and the old dog by the hearth wakes. You leave by the window with its teeth in your trouser leg.
opt.up.say.2 [ef29d5] = 一根撬锁针咔嚓一声断在抽屉锁里，壁炉边的老狗醒了。你从窗户逃出去，裤腿上挂着它的牙。

@event gy_ottilie_gone
# en: Room Seven
title [e4d0f3] = 七号房
# en: Room seven's door is open, and the room is made up fresh: clean sheets, an empty grate, no fern book, no sun hat. You ask the landlord where Miss Venn has gone. "Who?" he says, kindly, puzzled, wiping a glass. "We've no lady of that name. Never had." On the clean floor, under the bed, there's a pressed fern. {flag(moor_inn_key): In your pocket, the room key from the satchel in the peat has room seven's tag.|}
text [4fc6a9] = 七号房的门开着，房间刚收拾过：干净的床单，空空的壁炉，没有蕨叶书，没有遮阳帽。你问老板维恩小姐去哪儿了。“谁？”他擦着杯子，和气又困惑地说，“我们这儿没有叫这个名字的女士。从来没有。”在干净的地板上，床底下，有一片压干的蕨叶。{flag(moor_inn_key): 你口袋里那把从泥炭里的挎包里找到的房间钥匙，挂牌上写着七号房。|}
# en: An empty, freshly made-up inn bedroom with the door ajar, a number seven on the door, a pressed fern lying on the clean floor, a student in the doorway.
scene [97a773] = 一间刚收拾好、空无一人的客栈卧室，门半开着，门上写着数字七，干净的地板上躺着一片压干的蕨叶，一个学生站在门口。
# en: Say nothing, and go to the Marsh
opt.left.label [4a936d] = 什么也不说，去沼泽
# en: You say nothing. You pick up the fern, and walk out of the inn past the landlord's kind face, and keep walking, out of the village and down the causeway to the Marsh, to {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): your grandmother|the hedge-witch and her rue}.
opt.left.say.1 [e77283] = 你什么也没说。你捡起蕨叶，从老板那张和气的脸旁走出客栈，一直走，走出村子，顺着堤道下到沼泽，去找{at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 你的祖母|乡野女巫和她的芸香}。
# en: Call him a liar to his face
opt.right.label [53b71e] = 当面说他撒谎
# en: "She was here," you say, loud enough for the whole taproom. Nobody looks up. The landlord only smiles, sorry for you, and the room goes on with its evening as if you'd said nothing at all. You walk out with the fern in your fist, glad you said it, and with every eye in the valley on your back.
opt.right.say.1 [65e26b] = “她来过这儿，”你说，声音大得整个酒馆都听得见。没人抬头。老板只是微笑，替你难过，整个屋子照旧过它的夜晚，好像你什么也没说。你攥着蕨叶走出去，庆幸自己说了出来，背后是整个山谷的目光。

@event gy_witch_truth
# en: What the Rue Is For
title [dbffaf] = 芸香是做什么用的
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): Your grandmother is on the steps with the rue in her lap, waiting, as if she'd known you'd come today. "So," she says. "You've found it. I hoped you'd be cleverer and not."|The hedge-witch is on her steps with the rue in her lap, and for once she meets your eye. "So," she says. "They've taken the fern girl. Sit down."} Then she tells you: the Tenant, under the hollow hill on the moor, and the guest it's lent every seventh year. "They'll tell you the lent come home. They don't. They sit at its supper, not a day older, as long as the bargain holds." And the harvests, good, good, good.
text [90ddc0] = {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 你的祖母坐在台阶上，膝上放着芸香，像在等你，好像她早知道你今天会来。“好啊，”她说，“你找到了。我还盼着你聪明点，找不到呢。”|乡野女巫坐在台阶上，膝上放着芸香，这一回她直视着你。“好啊，”她说，“他们带走了那个找蕨的姑娘。坐下。”}然后她告诉你：山中房客，在荒原的空心山下，还有每逢第七年借给它的那位客人。“他们会告诉你，被借出去的人会回家。不会的。他们坐在它的晚宴上，一天也不老，只要约定还在。”还有收成，好，好，好。
# en: An old hedge-witch sitting on the steps of a stilt house over a reedy marsh at dusk, a bunch of rue in her lap, talking low to a student sitting below her.
scene [616fc8] = 黄昏时，一位老乡野女巫坐在芦苇沼泽上一座高脚屋的台阶上，膝上放着一束芸香，低声对坐在她下方的学生说话。
# en: Ask her to come with you
opt.left.label [8a9355] = 请她和你一起去
# en: She'll give you rue for the moor.
opt.left.hint [ff1305] = 她会给你带上荒原用的芸香。
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): "I've kept you out of it with rue every seventh year since you were born," she says. "I'm too old to go knocking. You aren't." She ties a sprig of rue into your buttonhole with red thread, very tight.|"I'm too old for knocking on hills," she says. "I keep who I can out of it with rue. That's my part." She ties a sprig into your buttonhole with red thread.} "Past the third cairn, to the door. It opens to them as knows what's behind it. Now you do."
opt.left.say.1 [9f5253] = {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): “从你出生起，每逢第七年我都用芸香把你挡在外面，”她说，“我老得敲不动山门了。你还年轻。”她用红线把一枝芸香系在你的扣眼上，系得很紧。|“我老了，敲不动山了，”她说，“我用芸香把能护住的人挡在外面。那是我的本分。”她用红线把一枝芸香系在你的扣眼上。}“过了第三座石堆，到那扇门。它为知道门后有什么的人打开。现在你知道了。”
# en: Ask how it could be broken
opt.right.label [48bfe6] = 问她怎么能破了它
# en: "Beat it at its own table, and it lets them all go, and the luck goes with them. Or give it better company than one sad stranger, if you can think of any." She spits into the marsh. "Or the man at the hall gets to it first. Past the third cairn, to the door. It opens to them as knows."
opt.right.say.1 [cf1b62] = “在它自己的席上打败它，它就会把他们全放了，福气也跟着走。或者给它比一个可怜的陌生人更好的陪伴，要是你想得出来的话。”她朝沼泽里啐了一口。“要不然，宅邸里那个人就先下手了。过了第三座石堆，到那扇门。它为知情的人打开。”

@event gy_hill_door_open
# en: The Door Stands Open
title [12fdc3] = 门敞开着
# en: The door in the hill is standing ajar. Through the gap comes warm gold light, and the smell of new bread and roasting, and the noise of a supper: knives, laughter, a fiddle playing a tune you nearly know. The sheaf knocker is warm under your hand.
text [444181] = 山里的那扇门半开着。门缝里透出温暖的金光，飘出新烤面包和烤肉的香味，还有晚宴的声响：刀叉声、笑声，一把提琴拉着一支你几乎认得的曲子。麦捆形的门环在你手下是温的。
# en: A low round oak door in the turf side of a hill on a foggy moor, standing ajar on warm golden light, the sound of a feast coming from inside, a student standing before it.
scene [b6f3ba] = 雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一座小山的草皮侧面有一扇低矮的圆橡木门，半开着，透出温暖的金光，里面传来宴会的声音，一个学生站在门前。
# en: Not tonight
opt.left.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不了
# en: You pull the door to, as gently as you can, and go back down off the moor. Behind you the fiddle plays on, and the fog closes over the hill like a lid.
opt.left.say.1 [160428] = 你尽可能轻地把门带上，走下荒原。身后提琴还在拉，雾像盖子一样合拢在山上。
# en: Go in
opt.right.label [7de3f2] = 进去
# en: You go in, ducking under the lintel, into the warm.
opt.right.say.1 [b7d4eb] = 你低头钻过门楣，走进那片温暖里。

@event gy_tenant_hall
# en: The Tenant's Table
title [d0da6e] = 山中房客的筵席
# en: A long hall under the hill, gold with lamplight, and a harvest supper laid down its whole length. Every stranger the valley ever lent it is here, in the clothes of every seventh year back, laughing, none a day older; near the bottom, in her sun hat, is Ottilie. At the head sits the Tenant, tall and wheat-crowned, with a face like a field seen from a moving cart. "A guest," it says, pleased, in a voice like harvest. "Sit."
text [14f0f4] = 山下一座长厅，灯火通明，金光一片，整条长桌上摆满了收获晚宴。山谷借给它的每一个陌生人都在这里，穿着每一个第七年的衣裳，笑着，一天也没老；靠近桌尾，戴着遮阳帽的，是奥蒂莉。桌首坐着山中房客，高大，戴着麦穗冠，一张脸像从行驶的马车上望见的田野。“一位客人，”它高兴地说，声音像收获。“坐。”
# en: A long golden hall inside a hill, a harvest supper laid for a hundred, guests in old-fashioned travelling clothes eating and laughing, and at the head of the table a tall figure crowned with wheat whose face is hard to look at.
scene [503941] = 山里一座金色的长厅，摆着能坐上百人的收获晚宴，穿着旧式旅行服的客人们边吃边笑，桌首坐着一个戴麦穗冠的高大身影，那张脸叫人难以直视。
# en: Walk out the way you came
opt.leave.label [c79fcb] = 原路走出去
# en: You don't sit. You walk back down the whole length of the table, past Ottilie, who doesn't know you, and out into the fog, and the door swings to behind you. It will open again; you know that.
opt.leave.say.1 [8d6b01] = 你没坐下。你沿着整条长桌走回去，经过不认得你的奥蒂莉，走进雾里，门在你身后合上。它还会再开的；你知道。
# en: Break the bargain at its own table
opt.fight.label [ba6460] = 在它自己的席上破约
# en: The Tenant fights for its supper. Win, and the lent go free, and the luck goes with them.
opt.fight.hint [b7642d] = 山中房客会为它的晚宴而战。赢了，被借出去的人就自由了，福气也跟着走。
# en: The Tenant goes down among its own sheaves, and the lamps gutter, and the long table is suddenly only trestles in the dark. "Then go," it says, from everywhere, "all of you, and take your bad years with you." The guests are standing up, blinking, one by one.
opt.fight.say.1 [2b0f13] = 山中房客倒在自己的麦捆中间，灯火摇曳熄灭，长桌忽然只剩黑暗里的几张支架。“那就走吧，”它的声音从四面八方传来，“你们所有人，把你们的坏年景也带走。”客人们一个接一个站起来，眨着眼。
# en: It doesn't strike you so much as set you aside, like a plate it's finished with. You come round on the wet heather outside the shut door, with the fog coming down and no idea how long you've been there.
opt.fight.say.2 [d77a6e] = 它与其说是打了你，不如说是把你搁到了一边，像搁下一只用完的盘子。你醒来时躺在紧闭的门外湿漉漉的石楠丛里，雾正落下来，不知道自己在那儿躺了多久。
# en: Offer it better company
opt.bargain.label [b39947] = 给它更好的陪伴
# en: Persuade it: the whole valley at its table for one night every seventh year, in place of a lent stranger. What you know of its guests helps.
opt.bargain.hint [81ba78] = 说服它：每逢第七年，整个山谷来它的席上过一夜，代替一个被借出去的陌生人。你对它客人的了解会有帮助。
# en: {flag(gy_guest_book) or flag(gy_coats): You name its guests, from the book and the collars, and offer better:|You offer it better company than any one guest:} the whole valley every seventh year, keepers, children and fiddlers, one night, home by morning. The Tenant listens to the end, and laughs, a sound like a full barn. "Done," it says. "Bring the fiddlers."
opt.bargain.say.1 [28e7f6] = {flag(gy_guest_book) or flag(gy_coats): 你说出它的客人们的名字，从住客簿里、从衣领里，然后提出更好的：|你给它提出比任何一位客人都好的陪伴：}每逢第七年，整个山谷，守约人、孩子和提琴手，来一夜，天亮回家。山中房客听到最后，笑了，那声音像一座装满的谷仓。“成交，”它说，“把提琴手带来。”
# en: It listens, smiling, and when you're done it shakes its wheat-crowned head. "One guest is a guest," it says. "A crowd is a market." It shows you the door with a courtesy that's worse than anger, and the fog outside has teeth.
opt.bargain.say.2 [ad0266] = 它微笑着听，等你说完，摇了摇戴着麦穗冠的头。“一位客人是客人，”它说，“一群人是集市。”它客客气气地送你出门，那份客气比发怒还糟，门外的雾也长了牙。
# en: Give it the agent's offer
opt.agent.label [40f8a7] = 把代理人的条件给它
# en: A guest every year from the agent's hand, and the luck to follow his company's land. Gold, and Hollow.
opt.agent.hint [7ecbb4] = 每年一位由代理人亲手挑选的客人，福气跟着他公司的地走。金币，和空洞。
# en: You tell it the agent's terms: a guest every year instead of every seventh, and the luck to his company's land. The Tenant's eyes go bright and greedy, and the supper roars. "A generous master," it says. "Tell him yes." Ottilie, at the bottom of the table, laughs at something you'll never hear.
opt.agent.say.1 [23c509] = 你把代理人的条件告诉它：不是每七年，而是每年一位客人，福气归他公司的地。山中房客的眼睛亮起来，贪婪地闪着光，晚宴一片喧腾。“一位慷慨的主人，”它说，“告诉他，好。”桌尾的奥蒂莉为一件你永远听不见的事笑了。

@event gy_after_broken
# en: The Guests Come Out
title [d533cb] = 客人们出来了
# en: You lead them down off the moor in the late light: Ottilie in her sun hat, asking where her ferns are; a young man in a coat seven years out of date, asking what year it is; and the rest, in shirtsleeves, the scarecrows having their coats, back further than the hedges, quiet and amazed. Behind you, the hill's door is only turf.
text [b70520] = 你在傍晚的余光里领着他们走下荒原：戴遮阳帽的奥蒂莉问她的蕨叶在哪儿；一个穿着过时七年外套的年轻人问现在是哪一年；其余的人只穿着衬衫，外套都在稻草人身上，一个比一个久远，比树篱还要古老，安静而惊奇。在你身后，山上的门只剩草皮。
# en: Late light on a foggy moor, a straggle of dazed people in old-fashioned coats walking down off a hill towards a village, a young woman in a sun hat among them, a student leading them.
scene [1d8925] = 雾蒙蒙的荒原上的傍晚余光，一群穿着旧式外套、神情恍惚的人从山上朝村子走下来，其中有个戴遮阳帽的年轻女人，一个学生在前面领路。
# en: Walk them down to the inn
opt.left.label [933eb7] = 领他们下到客栈
# en: You walk them into the market village at dusk, and the whole green comes out to see. The landlord stands in his doorway with a glass in his hand and his kind face gone grey. Nobody says a word to you. They don't need to: the next mark on the harvest board will say it for them.
opt.left.say.1 [55b0b4] = 黄昏时你领着他们走进集镇，整片绿地的人都出来看。老板站在门口，手里拿着一只杯子，那张和气的脸变得灰白。没有人对你说一个字。他们不必说：收成板上的下一道记号会替他们说。
# en: Take them to the Marsh first
opt.right.label [702963] = 先带他们去沼泽
# en: You take them down the causeway to {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): your grandmother|the hedge-witch}, who has a pot on and blankets out as if she'd expected all of them for supper. She counts them as they come in, all of them, and then she sits down on her step and cries, which you'd never have thought she could.
opt.right.say.1 [65e24d] = 你领着他们顺着堤道去找{at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 你的祖母|乡野女巫}，她已经架上了锅，铺好了毯子，好像早就料到他们全都会来吃晚饭。她一个个数着进门的人，一个不少，然后坐在台阶上哭了，你从没想到她会哭。

@event gy_after_renewed
# en: Bring the Fiddlers
title [49cadd] = 把提琴手带来
# en: The lent walk down off the moor with you at dusk, Ottilie among them complaining about her ferns, and the villages come out to see. You tell the green what you promised the Tenant on their behalf. There's a long silence. Then the miller, of all people, starts to laugh, and fetches his fiddle.
text [f01e46] = 黄昏时，被借出去的人们跟着你走下荒原，奥蒂莉在其中抱怨她的蕨叶，两个村子的人都出来看。你告诉绿地上的人，你代他们向山中房客许下了什么。长久的沉默。然后，偏偏是磨坊主，笑了起来，去拿他的提琴。
# en: A village green at dusk, a startled crowd gathering round a student and a straggle of people in old coats coming down from the moor, a fiddler already tuning up.
scene [798790] = 黄昏的村中绿地，吃惊的人群围住一个学生和一群从荒原上下来、穿着旧外套的人，一个提琴手已经在调弦了。
# en: Tell the landlord himself
opt.left.label [1829f1] = 亲自告诉客栈老板
# en: You stand the landlord a pint at his own bar and tell him: every seventh year, the whole valley up the hill for one night, and home by morning. He drinks it slowly. "Better," he says at last, and puts the guest book on the fire, and you both watch it burn.
opt.left.say.1 [b261f2] = 你在老板自己的吧台上请他喝一品脱，告诉他：每逢第七年，整个山谷上山去一夜，天亮回家。他慢慢喝完。“这样更好，”他终于说，然后把住客簿扔进火里，你们俩一起看着它烧。
# en: Leave it to the valley
opt.right.label [b35700] = 交给山谷自己办
# en: You leave them to it. By morning the green's arguing about who'll bring what to the supper under the hill in seven years' time, as if it were a wedding. The harvest board's next mark is a good one, and next to it somebody has chalked a fiddle.
opt.right.say.1 [2cafa1] = 你让他们自己去办。到了第二天早上，绿地上的人已经在争论七年后山下的晚宴谁带什么，好像要办一场婚礼。收成板上的下一道记号是好的，旁边有人用粉笔画了一把提琴。

@event gy_after_sold
# en: The Agent's Gratitude
title [5570f8] = 代理人的谢意
# en: The man in good boots is waiting at the old hall's gate at dusk, as if he'd known. He doesn't ask; he only looks at your face, and smiles, and holds out a purse. "My principals are grateful," he says. {flag(gy_agent_paid): "You've been worth every coin."|} "The upland will do very well now." Behind him, on the moor, the fog sits on the hollow hill like a hand.
text [11a3d0] = 黄昏时，那个穿好靴子的人已经等在老宅邸门口，好像他早就知道。他没有问；他只看了看你的脸，笑了，递出一个钱袋。“我的上家很感激，”他说。{flag(gy_agent_paid): “你值得每一枚金币。”|}“高地现在会很兴旺。”在他身后的荒原上，雾像一只手似的按在空心山上。
# en: A smiling man in good city boots handing a heavy purse to a student at the gate of a shuttered manor at dusk, fog on the moor behind.
scene [945d8b] = 黄昏时，一个穿城里好靴子的男人微笑着在一座百叶窗紧闭的庄园门口把一只沉甸甸的钱袋递给一个学生，身后的荒原上起着雾。
# en: Take the purse
opt.left.label [499dd2] = 收下钱袋
# en: You take it. It's heavier than anything you've carried out of the moor. Walking back to the village you pass {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): your grandmother|the hedge-witch} on the causeway, and she spits on the ground at your feet and doesn't say a word.
opt.left.say.1 [9b36cc] = 你收下了。它比你从荒原带出来的任何东西都沉。走回村子的路上，你在堤道上遇见{at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 你的祖母|乡野女巫}，她朝你脚下的地上啐了一口，一个字也没说。
# en: Throw it at his feet
opt.right.label [bfcff3] = 把它扔在他脚下
# en: You throw it in the road. He picks it up without a word, brushes it off and puts it away, still smiling, and that's worse. It's done. Your gold or his, the Tenant will have a guest every year now, and Ottilie is still at the table.
opt.right.say.1 [99323e] = 你把它扔在路上。他一言不发地捡起来，掸掸灰收好，仍旧微笑着，这更糟。事情已经定了。不管是你的金币还是他的，山中房客如今每年都会有一位客人，而奥蒂莉还坐在那张桌边。

@event gy_thin_harvest
# en: A Cross on the Board
title [7c6d3e] = 板上的叉
# en: This summer's mark on the harvest board is a cross, the first in living memory. The carts coming in are half full; the barley's thin, and honest, the way only the upland's used to be. {at_home(): Your neighbours nod to you, and don't stop to talk, and your family's table is plainer this year.|The landlord serves you without a smile. Nobody stands you a drink.} Ottilie writes from the capital, about ferns.
text [971472] = 今年夏天收成板上的记号是一个叉，这是人们记忆里的头一回。运进来的大车只装了一半；大麦稀稀拉拉，老老实实，以前只有高地才这样。{at_home(): 邻居们冲你点点头，不停下来说话，你家今年的饭桌也简朴了些。|老板招呼你时不带笑。也没人请你喝一杯。}奥蒂莉从首都写信来，说的是蕨。
# en: A village green with an old chalk tally board on a market cross, the newest mark a chalk cross, a thin harvest on the carts, villagers glancing coldly at a student.
scene [4cbb60] = 村中绿地，集市十字碑上挂着旧粉笔计数板，最新的记号是一个粉笔叉，大车上装着稀薄的收成，村民们冷冷地瞥着一个学生。
# en: Help bring in what there is
opt.left.label [5f8545] = 帮着收回剩下的
# en: You put your back into the thin harvest with everyone else, sheaf by sheaf, and by dusk a few people are talking to you again, grudgingly. "Bad years come," the miller says, wiping his face, "and good years don't. Like everywhere else, then." It isn't quite forgiveness. It's close.
opt.left.say.1 [ca3483] = 你和大家一起一捆一捆地收这场薄收，出了力，到黄昏时已经有几个人勉强又和你说话了。“坏年景会来，”磨坊主擦着脸说，“好年景不会自己来。跟别处一样了。”这还不完全算原谅。但差不多了。
# en: Keep your head down
opt.right.label [b59315] = 低头避开
# en: You keep out of the way. The valley gets on with its first bad year in living memory without you, as best it can, and you hear this year's cross on the board talked about in every taproom, and your name with it.
opt.right.say.1 [9fa34e] = 你避开了。山谷在没有你的情况下尽力熬过它记忆里的第一个坏年景，你在每家酒馆都听见人们说起今年板上的那个叉，还有你的名字。

@event gy_hill_turf
# en: Only Turf
title [544272] = 只剩草皮
# en: Round the far side of the hollow hill, where the door was, there's only turf, and in the grass an iron knocker shaped like a sheaf, rusted through as if it had lain there a hundred years. The hill is cold under your hand. Somewhere a lark goes up, an ordinary bird on an ordinary moor.
text [41dc69] = 绕到空心山背后，原来门所在的地方，只剩草皮，草丛里躺着一只麦捆形的铁门环，锈透了，好像已经在那里躺了一百年。山在你手下是冷的。不知哪儿有一只云雀飞起来，普通荒原上的一只普通的鸟。
# en: The green turf side of a hill on a foggy moor where a door used to be, a rusted iron knocker shaped like a sheaf lying in the grass, a student sitting beside it.
scene [81a55f] = 雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一座小山的绿色草皮侧面，那里曾经有一扇门，草里躺着一只生锈的麦捆形铁门环，一个学生坐在旁边。
# en: Go home
opt.left.label [c93952] = 回家
# en: You leave the knocker where it lies and walk back down past the cairns. The fog lifts as you go, and for once the moor is only as big as it looks.
opt.left.say.1 [2cb652] = 你让门环留在原地，经过一座座石堆走下山。你走着走着，雾散了，荒原难得地只有它看上去那么大。
# en: Sit on the hill a while
opt.right.label [97bc94] = 在山上坐一会儿
# en: You sit on the cold turf over the empty hall until the damp gets into your bones, and feel nothing under you at all. It's the most peaceful the moor has ever been, and you walk home stiff.
opt.right.say.1 [449d45] = 你坐在空荡大厅上方冰冷的草皮上，直到湿气钻进骨头，脚下什么也感觉不到。这是荒原有史以来最安宁的时刻，你僵着身子走回家。
